---
import SiteLayout from "../layouts/SiteLayout.astro";

const today = new Date();
const yearsOfExperience = today.getFullYear() - 2009 - (today.getMonth() < 6 ? 1 : 0);
---

<SiteLayout title="About" type="WebSite">
  <article class="Page">
    <img
      class="d-block m-auto round"
      src="/public/Avatar.png"
      alt="Agustín Díaz"
      width="160"
      height="160"
    />
    <h1 class="Page__Title">About</h1>
    <p class="lead">
      My name is Agustín Díaz, and I’m a Senior Design Engineer at{" "}
      <a href="https://github.com/">GitHub</a>.
    </p>
    <p>
      I work across design and frontend engineering, with {yearsOfExperience} years of experience
      building for the web. I care about the details of an interface and the code behind it. I’ve
      previously worked at <a href="https://stripe.com/">Stripe</a>,{" "}
      <a href="https://newrelic.com/">New Relic</a>, and{" "}
      <a href="https://www.personio.com/">Personio</a>.
    </p>
    <p>
      I also spent time at <a href="https://www.recurse.com/">The Recurse Center</a>, sharpening my
      programming skills alongside some of the nicest, most talented people I’ve ever met.
    </p>
    <p>
      I started my career developing E-Commerce stores on NetSuite, later got acqu-hired and helped
      build from scratch the{" "}
      <a href="http://www.netsuite.com/portal/products/suitecommerce.shtml">SuiteCommerce</a>{" "}
      platform.
    </p>
    <p>
      In my spare time I enjoy reading books, cycling on the{" "}
      <a href="https://www.tripadvisor.com/ShowUserReviews-g294323-d2233045-r196103509-Rambla_de_Montevideo-Montevideo_Montevideo_Department.html">
        promenade
      </a>
      , or playing video (or board) games. I’m also a dad to a very active kid.
    </p>
    <p>
      My online handle <em>HiroAgustin</em> is a reference to the lovable spacetime traveling
      programmer/samurai <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hiro_Nakamura">Hiro Nakamura</a> and
      a nod to my gaming days.
    </p>
  </article>
</SiteLayout>
